    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d127">

                <pb facs="0240" n="228" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg228"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/4346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-01-12T17:00:00+00:00">January 12, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 12—4:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. This morning I had a conversation with Chautemps Minister of State on the
                    subject of the Moroccan difficulty. He said that he felt <pb facs="0241" n="229"
                        xml:id="pg229"/> Vienot<anchor n="22" xml:id="d127-f1"/> had made a mistake
                    in getting the French press so excited about the matter but added that he was
                    glad that Hitler had been pushed into making his declaration to François-Poncet.
                    He believed that the incident could be considered closed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d127-f1" n="22" xml:id="d127-f1-content">
                <p>P. Vienot, French Under Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
